What is Streaming Inference?
Streaming inference is a type of ML inference that involves processing data as it is generated, in real-time. This approach is different from traditional batch processing, where data is collected and processed in batches. In streaming inference, the model receives a continuous stream of data, which it analyzes and generates predictions or insights on the fly.
