print(f'Pruned model accuracy: {accuracy:.2f}%')
```
In this example, we define a simple neural network model and train it on the MNIST dataset. We then prune the model by removing 10% of the weights with the lowest magnitude, which can help reduce memory usage. Finally, we evaluate the pruned model on the test dataset to ensure that it still maintains good accuracy.
