      "prompt": "Your second prompt",
      "max_tokens": 2048,
      "temperature": 0.5
    },
    ...
  ]
}
```
You can then send this JSON object in the body of a `POST` request to the `/batch` endpoint.

Here is an example using `curl`:
```bash
curl -X POST \
  https://api.openai.com/v1/engines/ada/batch \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' \
  -d '{
        "prompts": [
          {
            "prompt": "Tell me a joke.",
            "max_tokens": 2048,
            "temperature": 0.5
          },
          {
            "prompt": "Write a short story about a character who learns to play the guitar.",
            "max_tokens": 2048,
            "temperature": 0.5
          }
        ]
      }'
```
The response will be a JSON object with the following structure:
```json
